re\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7628) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12490F (12 threads) - 31.81 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am not sure that whether this is a bug or by design. The problem is that deterministic logic always considers the track, even when it's disabled. The current documentation only mentions that it takes the number of tracks into consideration, but does not specify whether it considers disabled tracks or not. If this is intended (not a bug), the documentation should mention it. (I can add a note later if needed.)\n\n#### Demostration video:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d04a0d93-e45d-4d66-ad1a-ebec4fd67afc\n\nIn the demonstration, even though I disabled the modulate track in the RESET animation, when deterministic blending is enabled, switching to other animations still modifies the Sprite's modulate.\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[deterministic_2025-12-18_21-17-11.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24236183/deterministic_2025-12-18_21-17-11.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/user